<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed weaker at -0.67 pct from parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed weaker at -0.67 pct from parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.4855 to the dollar, down from 3.4735 on Monday and at 1.8555 to the mark, up from 1.8565, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 0.67 percent below the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, weaker than Monday's fix at -0.54 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
